Summary of changes to the original library
------------------------------------------

Modified files: __init__.py, _cache.py, _casambi.py, _client.py,
_discover.py, _encryption.py, _network.py, _operation.py, _unit.py, errors.py.

Added files: _transport.py, _transport_factory.py, _bleak_transport.py,
_esphome_transport.py, _homeassistant_transport.py, README.md.

Unchanged files: _constants.py, _keystore.py, _switch.py, py.typed.

Main changes:
- Device roles (light, motorized shade, motorized screen, sensor) inferred
  from each unit's controls, and a generic setControl() write API.
- On/off support for motorized shades and screens, and slider scaling that
  honours each control's min/max.
- Decoding of sensor controls (presence, illuminance and the round-robin
  sensor group), with read-only controls rejected on write.
- A Bluetooth transport abstraction (local bleak adapter, ESPHome proxy,
  Home Assistant).
- Disconnect detection restored so lost BLE links are reported, and
  per-packet logs moved from INFO to DEBUG.
- Typing, lint and test fixes.

The Home Assistant integration itself (the other files under
custom_components/casambi_bt/), the demo web app (demo/) and the tests
were written in this repository.

The full history of changes is in the Git log of
https://github.com/pierreburton91/casambi-bt.
